  "waivers": {
    "Utopia\\CLI\\Adapters\\Swoole::*": "Swoole process-pool adapter (Swoole\\Process\\Pool, coroutine runtime hooks, getNative() returning the pool): runtime plumbing with no Rust counterpart (CONVERSION.md section 6). Running the work in several workers with start and stop callbacks is utopia_cli::Workers."
  },
  "tests_waived": {},
  "quirks": [
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\CLI\\Task::__construct",
      "description": "Task's constructor does not call Hook's, so a task's action is null until action() sets one: calling it raises TypeError, which CLI::run() (catching \\Exception only) lets out without running the error hooks.",
      "case": "edge.json#a task without a callback escapes run()"
    }
  ],
  "deviations": [
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\CLI\\CLI::run",
      "php": "A param default that is a callable is passed to the validator and to the task as the closure itself (getParams() never calls it).",
      "reason": "utopia_cli resolves params like every server: a ParamDefault::Factory is called with the param's injections. A closure is not a value a Rust task can receive; cases use value defaults."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\CLI\\CLI::run",
      "php": "coerce() turns a string into a boolean only when the validator (inside any Nullable) is an instance of Utopia\\Validator\\Boolean.",
      "reason": "utopia_validators::Validator has no class identity: utopia_cli coerces when the validator's kind() is Type::Boolean, which only Boolean (and a Nullable around it) reports among the library's validators; a WhiteList or AnyOf built with the boolean type would be coerced too."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\CLI\\CLI::run",
      "php": "Callbacks are called with named arguments, so one that declares no parameter for a name (the default action of a Hook given params or injections) raises Error 'Unknown named parameter $<name>'.",
      "reason": "A Rust callback receives Arguments, which cannot reject a name; a hook's default action does nothing whatever it is given. Cases set an action on every hook that has params or injections."
    }
  ]
}
